303.m:
Ekarudra, Trinetra, Śrīkaṇṭha, and Śikhaṇḍin;
[Page 121]
in the intermediate directions beginning with the northeast are these Lords of Knowledge, seated on lotuses.

305.m:
Bhṛgu and sky, accompanied by blazing fire, Bhṛgu, fire, and armor, *phaṭ*.
Thus: *hūṃ phaṭ* to the thousand-spoked [discus]; *ā cakrāya svāhā* to the heart; *vi cakrāya* to the head;
*śikhā cakrāya*, then the armor; *vi cakrāya*, then the eye;
[Page 125]
